  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts kept unchanged; no parts added or dropped.",
   "The catalogue card for arduino-mkr-wan-1300 lists only power ports (GND, VCC, 5V, VIN, USB, BATT) and no digital pins. Digital pin 2 is used on both boards, as the images and sketches show, so it is referenced as port '2' even though it is not in the card.",
   "The breadboard images label the top block rows j-f and the bottom block e-a. This is the reverse of the catalogue's naming, so the image's top block is written as bank 'b' (rows f-j). Row f is next to the centre gap.",
   "Sender: the pushbutton in the image sits on the top block only, with one leg in column 5 and one in column 7, and not across the centre gap. I followed the image. Column 5 (1.l) goes to GND and column 7 (2.l) to pin 2. These are on opposite sides of the switch, so pressing the button pulls pin 2 low (INPUT_PULLUP).",
   "Receiver: the LED cathode (straight leg) is in column 6, which the black wire takes to GND. The LED anode (bent, longer leg) is in column 8 and goes to the resistor in 8-11 of row g. The green wire from pin 2 is in column 11. So the resistor is on the anode side.",
   "The resistor value is not given in the manual, so 220 ohm is assumed.",
   "Each antenna connects to its board through its own cable. The board card has no antenna port, so that edge has no port on the board side.",
   "The micro USB cables are not drawn in the images. Each is joined to its board's USB port, since the parts list requires them.",
   "The two circuits are separate builds, with no electrical link between them. LoRa radio is the only link."
  ]
 },
